Add the core-backed espota TCP transfer engine. Pure library
helper that consumes an already-authenticated, already-Begun
single-transfer OTA transaction on a caller-provided connected
TCP socket. Wi-Fi variants only (nanoc6-wifi, atoms3-lite-wifi);
nanoc6-thread never applies, compiles, links, or exposes any of
the code here.

Compatibility reference: Arduino-esp32 3.3 ArduinoOTA
_runUpdate loop (1460-byte chunk read -> Update.write ->
decimal-ACK printf; ACK re-send x 3 on receive timeout; final
"OK" + restart). This helper mirrors the wire behaviour but
stays confined to the transfer itself.

Scope, kept minimal (no UDP listener, no TCP connect, no task,
no app_main hook, no service start, no authentication changes,
no restart, no mDNS, no HTTP change, no runtime caller in this
task):

  * NEW main/aliro_espota_transfer.h: declares
      esp_err_t AliroEspotaRunTransfer(int sock,
          const aliro_espota_invitation_t *invitation);
    plus size constants: 1460-byte buffer, ACK-retry cap 3,
    5-second bounded rx / tx timeouts.

  * NEW main/aliro_espota_transfer.cpp: implements the loop:
      - One fixed static 1460-byte receive buffer (static_
        assert-pinned). No heap; no per-chunk allocation.
      - SO_RCVTIMEO / SO_SNDTIMEO applied to the caller-
        provided socket before any recv / send.
      - recv() wrapper: transparent EINTR retry; EAGAIN /
        EWOULDBLOCK -> timeout sentinel; other error ->
        -1; EOF -> 0.
      - Per chunk: exactly one AliroLocalOtaWrite call, then a
        streaming MD5 update, then a decimal chunk-size ACK
        via snprintf("%zu") + send_all (no delimiter, matches
        ArduinoOTA's client.printf("%" PRIu32, written)).
      - Receive timeout: if a previous successful chunk
        produced an ACK, retransmit the SAME last decimal ACK
        without calling AliroLocalOtaWrite again, up to
        kAliroEspotaTransferMaxAckRetries = 3.
        Initial timeout, exhausted retries, real socket error,
        or clean EOF before invitation->size are all failures.
      - Final 16-byte MD5 compared to invitation->md5 BEFORE
        AliroLocalOtaFinish; on mismatch abort with
        ESP_ERR_INVALID_CRC.
      - AliroLocalOtaAbort ownership rules, per assignment
        and reviewer corrections:
          * ONE contract: the caller ALWAYS has an active
            AliroLocalOtaBegin transaction open before every
            call. The later service validates inputs and does
            NOT call this helper on validation failure. So
            invalid arguments detected here (sock < 0,
            invitation == nullptr, defensive-only
            invitation->size == 0) MUST call AliroLocalOtaAbort
            EXACTLY ONCE before returning ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG.
            No "no core action" path exists.
          * Called EXACTLY ONCE on any transport-layer / MD5
            failure while the core transaction is still open
            (setsockopt, initial recv timeout, exhausted ACK
            retries, real recv error, EOF short body, MD5
            update / finish failure, ACK-send failure, final
            MD5 mismatch).
          * NEVER called after AliroLocalOtaWrite or
            AliroLocalOtaFinish returns != ESP_OK: those core
            methods already consume + release the transaction;
            a second Abort could race with a fresh Begin.
          * NEVER called on a Finish-success path, even if the
            final TCP "OK" send fails. The transaction is
            already committed; the caller decides whether to
            restart. Return ESP_FAIL, no restart.
      - Helper never calls AliroLocalOtaBegin, never closes the
        socket, and never restarts the device.

  * WIRE patch 0019 into nanoc6-wifi and atoms3-lite-wifi
    source_patches in firmware/variants.json.
    nanoc6-thread source_patches is unchanged.

Explicit non-goals for this patch: no UDP listener, no TCP
connect, no task, no app_main hook, no service start, no
authentication changes, no restart, no mDNS, no HTTP change,
no runtime caller, no cJSON, no new runtime dependency, no
partition change, no CMakeLists.txt change (SRC_DIRS "."
already picks up main/ .cpp files on Wi-Fi variants).

diff --git a/examples/door_lock/main/aliro_espota_transfer.h b/examples/door_lock/main/aliro_espota_transfer.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/door_lock/main/aliro_espota_transfer.h
@@ -0,0 +1,145 @@
+/*
+   Core-backed espota TCP transfer engine for the Aliro door-lock
+   reader firmware. Compiled and linked only on the Wi-Fi variants
+   (nanoc6-wifi and atoms3-lite-wifi); the Thread variant never
+   applies, compiles, or links this module.
+
+   Scope, and only this scope: a pure library helper that consumes
+   an already-authenticated, already-Begun single-transfer OTA
+   transaction. It runs the wire protocol against a connected TCP
+   socket the caller passes in. It opens no sockets, spawns no
+   tasks, hooks into no app_main, starts no service, changes no
+   authentication, does not restart the device, and does not
+   touch mDNS or HTTP.
+
+   A later patch will supply a UDP invitation listener + TCP
+   receiver task that calls this helper after authentication.
+
+   Concurrency: single-caller-per-transaction. The core's busy
+   guard is already held when this helper runs.
+*/
+
+#pragma once
+
+#include <esp_err.h>
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+#include "aliro_espota_protocol.h"
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+// Sizes.
+enum {
+    /*
+       One TCP MSS on a typical ESP-IDF Wi-Fi stack. The ArduinoOTA
+       3.3 reference uses exactly the same static 1460-byte buffer.
+       No heap; no per-chunk allocation.
+    */
+    kAliroEspotaTransferBufBytes      = 1460,
+    /*
+       Number of times a chunk-size ACK is re-sent on receive
+       timeout after a successful write, matching the ArduinoOTA
+       reference. No further receive attempts are made on the
+       retry path; the helper only retransmits the last ACK.
+    */
+    kAliroEspotaTransferMaxAckRetries = 3,
+    /*
+       Bounded per-recv and per-send socket timeouts, in seconds.
+       The receive timeout is what drives the ACK-retry decision;
+       the send timeout bounds each ACK / final "OK" send.
+    */
+    kAliroEspotaTransferRxTimeoutSec  = 5,
+    kAliroEspotaTransferTxTimeoutSec  = 5,
+};
+
+/*
+   Run the espota body transfer over an already-connected TCP
+   socket. The caller has ALREADY:
+     * completed authentication (typically via
+       AliroEspotaVerifyAuth), and
+     * successfully called AliroLocalOtaBegin(invitation->size).
+
+   This helper CONSUMES that active core transaction. On every
+   return path from this helper the core's shared busy guard has
+   been released — either by successful Finish (return ESP_OK
+   after "OK" send), or by Abort here (HTTP-layer failures
+   listed below), or by Write / Finish themselves on their own
+   errors (this helper never re-Aborts after a core-method
+   error).
+
+   Ownership rules for AliroLocalOtaAbort inside this helper:
+
+     * Called EXACTLY ONCE, before returning, when the core
+       transaction is still open and one of the following
+       transport-layer failures occurs:
+         - setsockopt on the caller-provided socket fails
+         - streaming MD5 setup fails
+         - receive timeout when no successful ACK has been sent
+           yet (initial timeout)
+         - receive timeout after the ACK-retry cap
+         - real recv() error other than EINTR / EAGAIN
+         - clean EOF before invitation->size bytes are received
+         - streaming MD5 update fails
+         - ACK send fails after a successful Write
+         - streaming MD5 finalise fails
+         - final 16-byte MD5 does not match invitation->md5
+
+     * NEVER called after AliroLocalOtaWrite or
+       AliroLocalOtaFinish returns != ESP_OK: those core methods
+       already consume the transaction and release the shared
+       busy guard, and a second Abort could race with a fresh
+       Begin from another caller (see aliro_local_ota
+       ownership).
+
+     * NEVER called on a Finish success path, even if the final
+       TCP "OK" send fails. The transaction is already committed
+       and the boot partition is set; the caller decides whether
+       to reboot separately. The helper returns ESP_FAIL in that
+       case.
+
+   The helper has ONE contract: the caller has ALWAYS successfully
+   called AliroLocalOtaBegin(invitation->size) before every call.
+   The later service is responsible for validating its inputs and
+   for NOT calling this helper when validation fails. Because the
+   helper always inherits an active transaction, any invalid
+   argument detected here (sock < 0, invitation == nullptr, or a
+   defensive-only invitation->size == 0) must NOT leak a busy
+   transaction: the helper calls AliroLocalOtaAbort EXACTLY ONCE
+   and then returns ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG.
+
+   The helper never calls AliroLocalOtaBegin, never closes the
+   socket, and never restarts the device. Later service code
+   owns those actions.
+
+   Returns:
+     * ESP_OK               on success (transfer complete, MD5
+                            matched, Finish succeeded, final
+                            "OK" sent fully)
+     * ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG  invalid argument — the inherited
+                            active core transaction is aborted
+                            EXACTLY ONCE before this return
+                            (single ownership contract; no
+                            "no-core-action" path exists)
+     * ESP_ERR_TIMEOUT      receive timeout (initial or after
+                            ACK-retry cap); Aborted
+     * ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE clean EOF before invitation->size;
+                            Aborted
+     * ESP_ERR_INVALID_CRC  final MD5 mismatch; Aborted
+     * ESP_FAIL             other transport / crypto failure;
+                            Aborted (except a final "OK" send
+                            failure after Finish success, which
+                            returns ESP_FAIL WITHOUT Abort — the
+                            transaction is already committed)
+     * pass-through esp_err_t from AliroLocalOtaWrite /
+       AliroLocalOtaFinish on their own failures; NO extra Abort
+       (those core methods already consumed the transaction)
+*/
+esp_err_t AliroEspotaRunTransfer(int sock,
+                                 const aliro_espota_invitation_t *invitation);
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
diff --git a/examples/door_lock/main/aliro_espota_transfer.cpp b/examples/door_lock/main/aliro_espota_transfer.cpp
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/door_lock/main/aliro_espota_transfer.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,284 @@
+/*
+   Core-backed espota TCP transfer engine. Wi-Fi variants only
+   (nanoc6-wifi, atoms3-lite-wifi); the Thread variant never
+   applies, compiles, or links this file.
+
+   Compatibility reference: Arduino-esp32 3.3 ArduinoOTA
+   _runUpdate loop (chunk read -> Update.write -> decimal-ACK
+   printf, ACK re-send x 3 on receive timeout, final "OK" +
+   restart). This helper mirrors the wire behaviour but stays
+   confined to the transfer itself: no socket open / close,
+   no restart, and it never calls AliroLocalOtaBegin.
+
+   State ownership is documented in aliro_espota_transfer.h.
+   In short:
+     * Transport-layer / MD5 failure with the core transaction
+       still open -> AliroLocalOtaAbort exactly once.
+     * AliroLocalOtaWrite or AliroLocalOtaFinish returning an
+       error consumes the transaction itself; the helper does
+       NOT re-Abort.
+     * A failed final "OK" send after Finish success returns
+       ESP_FAIL WITHOUT Abort and WITHOUT restart; the
+       transaction is already committed.
+*/
+
+#include "aliro_espota_transfer.h"
+
+#include <errno.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <sys/socket.h>
+#include <sys/time.h>
+
+#include <esp_err.h>
+#include <esp_log.h>
+
+#include <mbedtls/md5.h>
+
+#include "aliro_local_ota.h"
+
+namespace {
+
+const char *TAG = "aliro_espota_xfer";
+
+/*
+   Fixed static receive buffer. Exactly 1460 bytes: one TCP MSS
+   on a typical ESP-IDF Wi-Fi stack, same as the ArduinoOTA
+   reference. No heap; no per-chunk allocation.
+*/
+static_assert(kAliroEspotaTransferBufBytes == 1460,
+              "espota receive buffer must be exactly 1460 bytes");
+uint8_t s_rx_buf[kAliroEspotaTransferBufBytes];
+
+/*
+   Apply per-socket receive and send timeouts so recv() returns
+   EAGAIN / EWOULDBLOCK on a stalled peer and send() cannot block
+   forever. Returns true on success.
+*/
+bool set_socket_timeouts(int sock) {
+    struct timeval rxto = { kAliroEspotaTransferRxTimeoutSec, 0 };
+    struct timeval txto = { kAliroEspotaTransferTxTimeoutSec, 0 };
+    if (setsockopt(sock, SOL_SOCKET, SO_RCVTIMEO, &rxto, sizeof(rxto)) != 0) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    if (setsockopt(sock, SOL_SOCKET, SO_SNDTIMEO, &txto, sizeof(txto)) != 0) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
+/*
+   Send exactly `len` bytes; retry on EINTR and on partial
+   sends. Returns true on complete send, false on error (bounded
+   by SO_SNDTIMEO).
+*/
+bool send_all(int sock, const void *buf, size_t len) {
+    const uint8_t *p = static_cast<const uint8_t *>(buf);
+    while (len > 0) {
+        ssize_t n = send(sock, p, len, 0);
+        if (n < 0) {
+            if (errno == EINTR) continue;
+            return false;
+        }
+        if (n == 0) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        p   += static_cast<size_t>(n);
+        len -= static_cast<size_t>(n);
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
+/*
+   Receive at most `cap` bytes into `buf`.
+   Returns:
+     n >= 1  bytes received
+     0       clean EOF
+    -1       real socket error (not EINTR / EAGAIN)
+    -2       receive timeout (EAGAIN / EWOULDBLOCK)
+   EINTR is retried transparently.
+*/
+ssize_t recv_some(int sock, void *buf, size_t cap) {
+    while (true) {
+        ssize_t n = recv(sock, buf, cap, 0);
+        if (n >= 0) return n;
+        if (errno == EINTR) continue;
+        if (errno == EAGAIN || errno == EWOULDBLOCK) return -2;
+        return -1;
+    }
+}
+
+/*
+   Format the espota decimal chunk-size ACK. Mirrors
+   ArduinoOTA's client.printf("%" PRIu32, written) — no
+   delimiter, no leading zeros, no sign. Returns the number of
+   ASCII bytes written, or -1 on overflow.
+*/
+int format_ack(size_t written, char *out, size_t cap) {
+    int n = snprintf(out, cap, "%zu", written);
+    if (n <= 0 || static_cast<size_t>(n) >= cap) return -1;
+    return n;
+}
+
+}  // namespace
+
+esp_err_t AliroEspotaRunTransfer(int sock,
+                                 const aliro_espota_invitation_t *invitation) {
+    /*
+       Ownership contract (single form): the caller ALWAYS has
+       an active AliroLocalOtaBegin transaction open when
+       calling this helper. Therefore any invalid argument
+       detected here MUST NOT leak a busy transaction — call
+       AliroLocalOtaAbort exactly once before returning. The
+       later service is responsible for validating inputs and
+       for NOT calling this helper when its own validation
+       fails; this branch is only defensive.
+    */
+    if (sock < 0 || invitation == nullptr ||
+        invitation->size == 0) {
+        AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    }
+
+    if (!set_socket_timeouts(sock)) {
+        ESP_LOGE(TAG, "setsockopt timeouts failed: errno=%d", errno);
+        AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+        return ESP_FAIL;
+    }
+
+    mbedtls_md5_context md5_ctx;
+    mbedtls_md5_init(&md5_ctx);
+    if (mbedtls_md5_starts(&md5_ctx) != 0) {
+        mbedtls_md5_free(&md5_ctx);
+        AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+        return ESP_FAIL;
+    }
+
+    size_t total_read       = 0;
+    size_t last_ack_written = 0;
+    int    ack_retries      = 0;
+
+    while (total_read < invitation->size) {
+        size_t want = invitation->size - total_read;
+        if (want > sizeof(s_rx_buf)) {
+            want = sizeof(s_rx_buf);
+        }
+        ssize_t n = recv_some(sock, s_rx_buf, want);
+
+        if (n == -2) {
+            /*
+               Receive timeout. If a previous successful write
+               produced an ACK, retransmit that same decimal
+               ACK (mirrors ArduinoOTA's Try[N]: <written>
+               path). Do NOT call AliroLocalOtaWrite here — the
+               helper only retransmits the last ACK. Cap at
+               kAliroEspotaTransferMaxAckRetries.
+            */
+            if (last_ack_written > 0 &&
+                ack_retries < kAliroEspotaTransferMaxAckRetries) {
+                char ack[16];
+                int alen = format_ack(last_ack_written, ack, sizeof(ack));
+                if (alen < 0 ||
+                    !send_all(sock, ack, static_cast<size_t>(alen))) {
+                    mbedtls_md5_free(&md5_ctx);
+                    AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+                    return ESP_ERR_TIMEOUT;
+                }
+                ack_retries++;
+                continue;
+            }
+            mbedtls_md5_free(&md5_ctx);
+            AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+            return ESP_ERR_TIMEOUT;
+        }
+        if (n < 0) {
+            mbedtls_md5_free(&md5_ctx);
+            AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+            return ESP_FAIL;
+        }
+        if (n == 0) {
+            /*
+               Clean EOF before invitation->size — the peer
+               closed. Treat as short body.
+            */
+            mbedtls_md5_free(&md5_ctx);
+            AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+            return ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE;
+        }
+
+        /*
+           Single AliroLocalOtaWrite call per received chunk.
+           On core failure, AliroLocalOtaWrite already consumed
+           the transaction and released the busy guard; do NOT
+           call AliroLocalOtaAbort here (would race with a fresh
+           Begin from another caller).
+        */
+        esp_err_t wr = AliroLocalOtaWrite(s_rx_buf, static_cast<size_t>(n));
+        if (wr != ESP_OK) {
+            mbedtls_md5_free(&md5_ctx);
+            return wr;
+        }
+
+        // Update the streaming MD5 AFTER a successful Write.
+        if (mbedtls_md5_update(&md5_ctx, s_rx_buf,
+                               static_cast<size_t>(n)) != 0) {
+            mbedtls_md5_free(&md5_ctx);
+            AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+            return ESP_FAIL;
+        }
+
+        // Send the decimal chunk-size ACK (no delimiter).
+        char ack[16];
+        int alen = format_ack(static_cast<size_t>(n), ack, sizeof(ack));
+        if (alen < 0 ||
+            !send_all(sock, ack, static_cast<size_t>(alen))) {
+            mbedtls_md5_free(&md5_ctx);
+            AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+            return ESP_FAIL;
+        }
+
+        last_ack_written = static_cast<size_t>(n);
+        ack_retries      = 0;
+        total_read      += static_cast<size_t>(n);
+    }
+
+    // Received exactly invitation->size bytes. Finalise the
+    // streaming MD5 and compare BEFORE Finish so a mismatched
+    // image never reaches esp_ota_set_boot_partition.
+    uint8_t md5_out[kAliroEspotaMd5Bytes];
+    if (mbedtls_md5_finish(&md5_ctx, md5_out) != 0) {
+        mbedtls_md5_free(&md5_ctx);
+        AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+        return ESP_FAIL;
+    }
+    mbedtls_md5_free(&md5_ctx);
+
+    if (memcmp(md5_out, invitation->md5, kAliroEspotaMd5Bytes) != 0) {
+        AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_CRC;
+    }
+
+    /*
+       Finish consumes / releases the transaction on ANY return,
+       so a Finish failure must NOT be followed by Abort.
+    */
+    esp_err_t fx = AliroLocalOtaFinish();
+    if (fx != ESP_OK) {
+        return fx;
+    }
+
+    /*
+       Only now send the final espota "OK" response. If the send
+       itself fails, return ESP_FAIL but do NOT restart and do
+       NOT Abort: the transaction is already committed and the
+       boot partition is set. The caller decides what to do
+       (log + close socket + optionally restart at a later
+       stage).
+    */
+    static const char kOk[] = "OK";
+    if (!send_all(sock, kOk, 2)) {
+        return ESP_FAIL;
+    }
+
+    return ESP_OK;
+}
